{
  "rationale": "The plant models the robot's motion and perception interface, exposing all controllable and uncontrollable events. The specification encodes a conservative, coverage-biased exploration policy: random_walk is used in clear, safe states; move_forward is used only in a short commit state; obstacle events force recovery via directed turns (not full_rotate unless both sides are blocked); recovery states return to exploration as soon as path_clear is observed. All obstacle states allow only one recovery action, and no obstacle state enables forward or random_walk. The design is deterministic, safe, and alternates between exploration and recovery as required.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant for motion/perception interface; all events exposed",
    "Specification encodes safe, coverage-biased exploration: random_walk in clear, move_forward in commit, directed turns for obstacle recovery, full_rotate only as last resort"
